parley-deck/ideas/protocol-restructure-appendices/signoffs/hermes-1.md:3:Notes: Consensus faithfully captures my round-01 position on all five points. D1 (keep-numbers-relocate) correctly reflects my argument that cross-refs survive by construction and renumbering rewrites content lines. D2 (minimal move: only §9 past §10) correctly attributes the single-block-move insight to me and matches my proposed target order exactly (§8 → §10 → §9 → §11). D3 (no Appendices banner) correctly attributes my purity argument against adding a content line. D4 includes all four of my verification gates (sorted-diff empty, drift guard green, ref audit, protocolSha256 refresh) plus two additional consistent checks (skill fallback identity, anchor count re-confirmation) that strengthen without contradicting. D5 scope boundaries match my §4-505-lines analysis. The agreed trade-off (non-sequential §8→§10→§9→§11) is the one I accepted. The change is a provably-content-preserving pure block reorder with no additions, deletions, or text modifications — safe to implement.
